+### The 100320 runs store triplets
+
+`set_schedule` and the calendar wrote `[[minute,setpoint],...]` to every program
+run. On the runs at 100320 and 100327 the device refuses that with
+"execution ended in state 4". Atlantic describes 100320 as "the start time and
+the extended state of the schedule transition", and the app writes
+`[[minute,setpoint,0],...]` there, padded with `[0,0,0]`.
+
+Measured 2026-11-26 on two Thermor Riva 5 (model 1560, product 53, Wi-Fi,
+no bridge): five refusals in the diagnostics dump, the last one with no 00:00
+slot, so the missing 00:00 is not the cause. With triplets the write is
+accepted and `get_schedule` reads the same seven days back, on both devices.
+
+`build_matrix` takes `extended` and `stores_extended(first)` decides it from
+the run's first id. The 196 and 203 runs keep pairs : nothing measured says
+they changed. A device that stores 100320 but accepts pairs, if one exists,
+is not known ; the extra zero is what the app sends.
+
